From cb70393f04694200d6e97822350e9659a5b3d0d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ozark <ozark@localhost>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:56:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Settings > Lighting: controller port override and strip setup

The Interior and Exterior Lighting tabs only set looks; the lighting
controller behind them (Ozark's ozark-lightd, org.ozark.Lighting1) is
configured here: its status, a serial port override (normally 'auto'),
each strip's data pin, LED count, colour order, RGBW, data speed,
direction and colour test, the brightness cap and music sensitivity.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [needs Ozark OS's lighting service]
---
